    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0860" n="1818" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1818"/>

                <head>No. 66.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 5, 1888</date>.
                        (Received December 5.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the case of the seizure
                    of four British sealing ships in Behring Sea, I have the honor to inclose, for
                    convenience of reference, copy of Lord Sackville’s dispatch of October 12<anchor
                        n="*" xml:id="d521-f1"/> (without its inclosure) to your Department, as I
                    have been instructed by the Marquis of Salisbury to call your attention to the
                    fact that up to the present no answer has been received, and to beg the favor of
                    an early reply.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur Herbert</hi></signed>,<lb/>For
                            <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. H.
                    Herbert.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
